[[:db/retract 17592186060412 :question/answer-fields 17592186059094] {:db/id 17592186059690 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2bdcd5e4-a0e7-512a-97bb-f847c06388f4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-2bdcd5e4-a0e7-512a-97bb-f847c06388f4" :question/id #uuid "2bdcd5e4-a0e7-512a-97bb-f847c06388f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-82451" :question/problem "Simplify the statement $¬(P∧Q)⇒(P∧R).$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that\n\n$$\n¬(P∧Q)⇒(P∧R)≡¬(¬(P∧Q))∨(P∧R).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n¬(¬(P∧Q))∨(P∧R)≡(P∧Q)∨(P∧R).\n$$\n\nFinally, by the distributive laws, we have\n\n$$\n(P∧Q)∨(P∧R)≡P∧(Q∨R).\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $P∧(Q∨R).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f19fca36-2b89-53ba-85fc-7765f2211e66"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f19fca36-2b89-53ba-85fc-7765f2211e66" :answer-field/id #uuid "f19fca36-2b89-53ba-85fc-7765f2211e66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-be278a98-7931-527b-9249-5fe023ad7c54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-173a22f9-03eb-5f52-84a2-64add79bb270" "answer-be278a98-7931-527b-9249-5fe023ad7c54" "answer-666720f8-ee5e-5a0c-9eff-9b28566b29c6" "answer-2655898f-0ab3-55b9-b970-24883e6a1310" "answer-d2702799-977f-5026-b7cd-3d37fe168a4b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-173a22f9-03eb-5f52-84a2-64add79bb270" :answer/id #uuid "173a22f9-03eb-5f52-84a2-64add79bb270" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧(Q∧R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-be278a98-7931-527b-9249-5fe023ad7c54" :answer/id #uuid "be278a98-7931-527b-9249-5fe023ad7c54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧(Q∨R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-666720f8-ee5e-5a0c-9eff-9b28566b29c6" :answer/id #uuid "666720f8-ee5e-5a0c-9eff-9b28566b29c6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∧(Q∨¬R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2655898f-0ab3-55b9-b970-24883e6a1310" :answer/id #uuid "2655898f-0ab3-55b9-b970-24883e6a1310" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "P∨(Q∨R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d2702799-977f-5026-b7cd-3d37fe168a4b" :answer/id #uuid "d2702799-977f-5026-b7cd-3d37fe168a4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "¬P∧(Q∨R)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059688 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c4482556-1279-5932-bd2e-cbe957830200"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c4482556-1279-5932-bd2e-cbe957830200" :question/id #uuid "c4482556-1279-5932-bd2e-cbe957830200" :question/math-academy-id "q-182574" :question/problem "$\\,$ Either apologize, or she won't forgive you.\n\nWhich conditional statement is logically equivalent to the disjunctive statement above?" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote by $A$ and $B$ the following statements:\n\n- $A:$ Apologize.\n\n- $B:$ She won't forgive you.\n\nThen, our initial statement can be written as $A∨B,$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n¬A⇒B.\n$$\n\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $¬A:$ You don't apologize.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ If you don't apologize, then she won't forgive you.\n\n**Note**: \n\nUsing the word \"Either\" helps clarify that the sentence structure presents two alternatives and is particularly useful when employing the disjunctive form $(¬P∨Q)$ in conversational or formal English. So, the phrase effectively conveys that one of the two stated conditions will hold true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e83d217a-41be-555a-a16a-343371ec8880"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e83d217a-41be-555a-a16a-343371ec8880" :answer-field/id #uuid "e83d217a-41be-555a-a16a-343371ec8880" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-38c9c24e-3b55-56ca-86a7-b2ce01e8f281" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a2993367-1981-5e54-b3ef-99b9be03f44e" "answer-719cf9b3-0ac6-54a8-b955-880ab8843c40" "answer-8213100f-0dc7-5d4d-b8fd-6e029e273dc5" "answer-a2794c58-1f77-5658-9986-016411aec9fd" "answer-38c9c24e-3b55-56ca-86a7-b2ce01e8f281"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2993367-1981-5e54-b3ef-99b9be03f44e" :answer/id #uuid "a2993367-1981-5e54-b3ef-99b9be03f44e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Apologize, and she will forgive you." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-719cf9b3-0ac6-54a8-b955-880ab8843c40" :answer/id #uuid "719cf9b3-0ac6-54a8-b955-880ab8843c40" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "If you apologize, then she will forgive you." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8213100f-0dc7-5d4d-b8fd-6e029e273dc5" :answer/id #uuid "8213100f-0dc7-5d4d-b8fd-6e029e273dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "If you apologize, then she won't forgive you." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a2794c58-1f77-5658-9986-016411aec9fd" :answer/id #uuid "a2794c58-1f77-5658-9986-016411aec9fd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "If you don't apologize, then she will forgive you." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-38c9c24e-3b55-56ca-86a7-b2ce01e8f281" :answer/id #uuid "38c9c24e-3b55-56ca-86a7-b2ce01e8f281" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "If you don't apologize, then she won't forgive you." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-ad31faf4-6ba4-59e5-b6eb-0f068c9137a4" :activity/id #uuid "ad31faf4-6ba4-59e5-b6eb-0f068c9137a4" :activity/title "Logical Equivalence with Conditional Statements" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049805 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-12d4c7cd-cbe3-5cf6-98ac-5ef2b58306b0" "step-a4bf2a7e-915f-5aaa-9350-9113ac1d5a6e" "step-b4e7f46a-d2bb-5a13-8fe3-d393ec767bb7" "step-992a12e5-4030-5d06-bfe4-99bff662d13d" "step-ec1c